# Config fragment merged onto radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig.
#
# These four CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR* values are per-chip vendor DRAM
# calibration data -- Kconfig's own help text for them says "value from
# vendor DRAM settings". radxa-cubie-a5e_defconfig hardcodes ONE fixed set,
# but the Cubie A5E ships in 1GB/2GB/4GB LPDDR4x variants with different DRAM
# chips, and upstream's values only suit whichever reference unit was used to
# submit the board. On a real 1GB board (bean gosd-6pfn's bench session),
# upstream's values make U-Boot SPL's DRAM init fail outright:
#
#   DRAM:DRAM test failure at address 0x6fffffc0
#    0 MiB
#   ### ERROR ### Please RESET the board ###
#
# 0x6fffffc0 decodes exactly (mctl_calc_size(), dram_dw_helpers.c) as
# 0x40000000 + (1024MiB * 3/4) - 64: DRAM sizing correctly detects 1GiB is
# present, then the read-back check at the top of that range fails under the
# defconfig's tuned parameters -- a data-integrity failure, not a dead
# controller (bean gosd-84b8 has the full trace and root-cause analysis).
#
# The values below are read back from a working vendor bootloader on a 1GB
# board by the Armbian community and are hardware-verified here the same
# way: rebuilding U-Boot from gosd's identical pinned sources with only
# these four values changed took the board from halting in SPL to a clean
# `DRAM: 1024 MiB` and a full boot to /app, first try. Source:
# https://github.com/Guation/radxa-cubie-a5e-armbian-build/commit/202f1bf
#
# This has been verified on a 1GB board ONLY. The 2GB/4GB variants ship
# different DRAM chips and may still fail SPL DRAM init with these values --
# if you're running one, please get in touch (bean gosd-84b8) with whether it
# boots. Re-deriving values for another variant means reading tpr6/tpr10/
# tpr11/tpr12 back off that variant's own working vendor bootloader, the same
# way the Armbian community did for this one.
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x3a000000
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0x882f3333
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR11=0xe6e6e2e3
CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR12=0x38383031
